{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-163017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a thin rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $0\\le x\\le 1$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)=x-{x}^{3}.$ Given that the rod's mass is $\\frac{1}{4}$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=x-{x}^{3},\\,a=0,\\,b=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot (x-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}-{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{2}{15})}{(\\frac{1}{4})}=\\frac{8}{15}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9cd4762dda1c7018a6cc8a9c837a598527b4f70d5a4dae98bb0db25b86c8f21d"} {"question" "q-163017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{10}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{15}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{15}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a thin rod along the $x$-axis over the interval $0\\le x\\le 2$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)=8-{x}^{3}.$ Find the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass of the rod." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=8-{x}^{3},\\,a=0,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nSo, the mass of the rod is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}8-{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[8x-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =8\\cdot 2-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot (8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}8x-{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[4{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 4-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 32 \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{48}{5})}{12}=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9cd4762dda1c7018a6cc8a9c837a598527b4f70d5a4dae98bb0db25b86c8f21d"} {"question" "q-163026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A thin rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)=\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}},$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ is placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le 4,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. Find the moment of the rod about the origin." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}},\\,a=1,\\,b=4.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\cdot \\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{4}{x}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{4}{4}-\\frac{4}{1}) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $3\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9cd4762dda1c7018a6cc8a9c837a598527b4f70d5a4dae98bb0db25b86c8f21d"} {"question" "q-163037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "3\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "4.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163086" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/assets/32500120ed36acde90f5b27c44a6cf45f2d4766bacb5eb097debc0cd7117f27f.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163086" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}},\\,a=1,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{2}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163086" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9cd4762dda1c7018a6cc8a9c837a598527b4f70d5a4dae98bb0db25b86c8f21d"} {"question" "q-163086" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163086" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "3\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163086" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163087" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/assets/32500120ed36acde90f5b27c44a6cf45f2d4766bacb5eb097debc0cd7117f27f.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)={x}^{2}-x\\,\\text{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163087" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)={x}^{2}-x,\\,a=1,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\cdot ({x}^{2}-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{3}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3})-(\\frac{{1}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{34}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $\\frac{34}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163087" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9cd4762dda1c7018a6cc8a9c837a598527b4f70d5a4dae98bb0db25b86c8f21d"} {"question" "q-163087" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074110/state.json" "file_sha256" "4174a502e46b5e1778fc712b907f64c7430e6d1081ed909c1d594b4df0d432d1"} {"question" "q-163087" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "\\frac{25}{6}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "\\frac{34}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "\\frac{43}{9}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Develo